    "result_text": "The build is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event on the owner-create path.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n- **New `OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (`rest/controller/v1`) \u2014 an immutable `record` that serializes to the exact JSON shape `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}`. Being a record, the event can't be mutated after the create that produced it \u2014 the immutability an audit trail relies on. It builds the JSON via the project's `tools.jackson` (Jackson 3) `ObjectNode` so field order is fixed and the string escaping is correct.\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n  - Added a static `AtomicLong EVENT_SEQ` \u2014 the source of the monotonically increasing `seq`, bumped once per successful create.\n  - After the existing human-readable audit line, it now also emits the structured event: `AUDIT.info(event.toJson())`. (The single-argument `Logger.info(String)` logs the JSON literally \u2014 it does not treat the `{}` braces as SLF4J placeholders.)\n  - Added a `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` accessor that returns `owner.getCustomerCode()`. The event pulls its identifier through this one method, so the spec's forward path \u2014 when the customerCode is unified into the memberId \u2014 is a single-line change there, with no other call site affected.\n\n**Behavior notes:**\n- The event is emitted only on genuine creates. Idempotent-key replays return early (before this code), so they neither emit a new event nor advance `seq` \u2014 correct, since a replay isn't a new creation.\n- `customerCode`/`membershipLevel` are read *after* `saveOwner`, so the code is populated and the values match the audit line and the returned DTO.\n\nThe suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), and the emitted line confirms the shape:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```",
